    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests green).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipTier` field is a read-only, server-derived property on an owner, so I implemented it the same way the existing derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`) are handled in this Spring/MapStruct app:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` includes the field and it's documented in the API contract.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression and a `formatMembershipTier(owner)` default method implementing the rule: returns `\"SILVER\"` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, otherwise `\"BRONZE\"` (null-safe on both `namesakeCount` and `email`).\n\nThis matches the two acceptance tests: a unique owner (namesakeCount 0) with an email \u2192 `SILVER`; a unique owner with no email \u2192 `BRONZE`.",
